@startuml cls-authorization
title Class Diagram — Authorization

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle

class AppUser <<external — identity>> {
}

class Role {
  +roleId: Int
  +roleName: String
  +description: String
}

class Permission {
  +permissionId: Int
  +permissionName: String
  +description: String
}

class RolePermission {
  +roleId: Int
  +permissionId: Int
  +assignmentDate: DateTime
}

class UserRole {
  +userId: UUID
  +roleId: Int
  +assignmentDate: DateTime
}

Role "1" -- "0..*" RolePermission : role_permission.role_id FK
Permission "1" -- "0..*" RolePermission : role_permission.permission_id FK
Role "1" -- "0..*" UserRole : user_role.role_id FK
AppUser ..> UserRole : user_role.user_id\n(cross-context, no FK)

note right of Role
  RN-07: roles are global, no school_id. Seeds:
  Administrador, Instructor, Aprendiz (legacy
  SUPER_ADMIN/SCHOOL_ADMIN/INSTRUCTOR/STUDENT
  merged).
end note

note right of Permission
  Format context.resource:action, e.g.
  attendance.justification:approve.
  RN-09/RN-10: access depends on the assigned
  role's permissions.
end note

note bottom of RolePermission
  PK (role_id, permission_id).
end note

note bottom of UserRole
  PK (user_id, role_id). RN-07: every AppUser
  must have at least one role.
end note

note as N1
  All classes also carry the standard audit block
  (created_at/updated_at/deleted_at/created_by/
  updated_by/deleted_by/row_version) — omitted
  here for readability. See AGENTS.md §2.2 and
  06-data/domains/02-authorization.md for the
  column-level ER view.
end note

@enduml
